        'Automates six main workflows: feature, fix, spike, ship, audit, and quick.',
        'Detects the repo stack and adapts artifacts. Lucius is the only optional agent.',
      ],
    },
    {
      title: 'Operational summary for reconstruction',
      body:
        'The visible surface is 18 published commands and 10 agents, but the real system lives behind that: Python core, 10 hooks, SQLite memory, and an orchestrator that never delegates state.',
      bullets: [
        'Agents are discovered from agents/. plugin.json lists the 18 commands.',
        'Lucius is the only optional agent. Selina enters when there is a frontend.',
        'Quality gates are hard: evidence-guard and quality-gate stop progress if real proof is missing.',
        'Each phase can retry up to 5 times before escalation to the user.',
      ],
    },
    {
      title: 'Technology stack',
      body:
        'The project operates over separated but coordinated ecosystems: Python for orchestration and memory, Astro for public documentation, and native Node.js for Selina visual server.',
      bullets: [
        'The core uses Python 3.10+ for orchestrator, config_loader, memory, continuity, and hooks.',
        'The public website lives in static Astro with TypeScript and sitemap.',
        'Selina uses native Node.js modules: http, crypto, fs, and path, with no external dependencies.',
        'Development relies on pytest for Python and astro check for the website.',
      ],
    },
    {
      title: 'Layered architecture',
      body:
        'Commands, agents, core, hooks, MCP, and visual server are separated. Commands do not call agents directly: they activate the orchestrator, and Alfred decides what enters and in what order.',
      bullets: [
        'Visible commands -> orchestrator.py -> agents and phases.',
        'Hooks intercept SessionStart, SessionEnd, UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse, and PostToolUse.',
        'memory_server exposes MCP tools to query memory from any agent.',
        'Agents do not talk to each other; everything goes through Alfred and session state.',
      ],
    },
    {
      title: 'Persistence and database',
      body:
        'Persistent memory lives in .claude/alfred-memory.db. It is designed to be local, portable, and safe, not dependent on remote services or additional infrastructure.',
      bullets: [
        'Local SQLite with WAL mode and FTS5 search.',
        'Persistence of decisions, commits, iterations, and events.',
        '0600 permissions and sanitization with 13 regex patterns for secrets.',
        'Automatic schema migration and configurable purge with retention_days.',
      ],
    },
    {
      title: 'Business logic and quality gates',
      body:
        'The system solves a very concrete problem: stopping AI-driven development from skipping critical phases and closing work without enough security, QA, documentation, or evidence.',
      bullets: [
        'Without recorded evidence, a claim like “tests pass” does not count.',
        'Security Officer appears transversally in architecture, quality, and delivery.',
        'Selina visual phase activates only when the stack has frontend surface.',
        'User gates and automatic gates stay separated; autopilot never skips security or evidence.',
      ],
    },
    {
      title: 'Runtime and auxiliary components',
      body:
        'Beyond the core, the system adds operational pieces that make the flow usable day to day: continuity, inspectable memory, optional GitHub sync, and a visual server with timeout.',
      bullets: [
        'Continuity keeps progress, pause, retomar, and handoff without losing phase.',
        'Memory UI opens timeline, decisions, commits, and health over local SQLite.',
        'GitHub Sync mirrors local state to issues when shared tracking is useful.',
        'Selina visual server uses a 30-minute timeout and checks the parent process every 60 seconds.',
      ],
    },
    {
      title: 'Boot and reconstruction',
      body:
        'You do not need complex infrastructure to rebuild or boot it, but you do need to respect the rules that make the system reliable.',
      bullets: [
        'Claude Code, Python 3.10+, and Node.js must be available in the environment.',
        'SQLite memory is created when memory is enabled in /alfred-dev:ajustes.',
        'map-codebase, discuss, and quick generate useful context so memory does not start empty.',
        'The most expensive mistake would be breaking agent isolation or allowing another layer to replace the orchestrator as the source of truth.',
      ],
    },
  ],
  principles: [
    'The orchestrator is the only source of truth for state.',
    'Quality gates are impassable without evidence.',
    'Security appears transversally in architecture, quality, and delivery.',
    'Memory and continuity prevent context loss between sessions.',
    'Core agents must not be invoked outside the orchestrated flow.',
  ],
};
const alfredOriginEn = {
  kicker: 'History and motivation',
  badge: 'Origin',
  lead: 'The idea was to build the assistant a developer would actually want beside them.',
  summary:
    'Alfred Dev starts from a very simple intuition: the best assistant for software development is not the one that talks the most, but the one that understands context, imposes order, solves things well, and keeps the level high when work gets hard.',
  highlights: [
